WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.803
-This film is shot
abroad in London, Morocco.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:07.073
I imagine you were away from
home for a long time.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.576
-Yeah, that was,
what was it like,

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.477
three months or so in total.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.679
It was definitely the longest
that I've ever been

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:14.881
away from home.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:18.451
So, I definitely found myself
getting homesick

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.986
from time to time.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.954
And that honestly,
I feel like was

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:25.624
one of the toughest things about
the project, actually.

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:28.161
Especially being in London,
where it's like --

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.762
I don't know.
London to me felt like

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.398
an alternate dimension,
like in the "Spider-verse"

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.233
or something where it's like,

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.202
most things are the same,

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.439
but there's just things that are
just slightly different enough

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.740
to make you
a little uncomfortable.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.242
Like, "Wait, where am I?"

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:45.378
-You know, one of the other
things that I talked about

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.214
last night with Charlize,
was the fact this is a film

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.617
that had a female director,
female producers,

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.952
obviously two female stars.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.288
Was that a fun environment
to be part of?

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.089
-Yeah, definitely.

00:00:57.089 --> 00:01:00.627
And I mean, just cool to be
in an environment where

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.563
so many women were leading.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:07.933
And now to see --
I mean, it's crazy, you know,

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:11.070
that it's still such a topic
of conversation,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.540
like as if though women aren't
leading every day,

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.144
women aren't phenomenal
directors and action heroes

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.746
every single day.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.581
So, I'm hoping this will,
I don't know,

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:25.951
give us a good push in the
direction of it becoming

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:29.088
more of the norm
as it should be.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.957
-There was obviously no premiere
for this film.

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:33.926
Did you watch it
with your family

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.295
right as it came live
on Netflix?

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:38.831
-I did. I did.
Which was awesome.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:42.668
You know, as much as I love
a big premiere moment,

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:46.172
it did make this, you know,
feel that much more special

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.975
because, I mean, it's no secret,
this is a huge milestone

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.543
for my career.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.079
And to be able to celebrate
that,

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.613
you know, with the people
who have been

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:57.282
a part of this journey with me
from the very beginning,

00:01:57.282 --> 00:01:58.984
since I was 7 years old
and said,

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:01.187
"Hey, I want to act,"

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:04.090
it actually made it, you know,
that much more special.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.793
-And tell me, how is your mom

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.828
with the violence
in the film?

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.297
Because you know, there's --
and you particularly, you know,

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.466
you take it pretty badly
a few times.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.102
-Yeah.
She was fine.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.404
It honestly was my dad.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.706
Like, I mean, I guess spoiler.
Whatever, it's on Netflix.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:23.943
It's all good,
but so my first death --

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:27.079
my mom, she took it, you know,
a little uncomfortable.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.481
But my dad, I had to like go
up to him and like rub him

00:02:29.481 --> 00:02:32.585
on his back like, "Hey, dad.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:33.953
I'm okay."

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.722
Just kind of like silently
sniffling.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:38.190
But, yeah.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.960
-I imagine violence
won't be an issue

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.329
in another film of yours that,
maybe language will be an issue

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:46.232
for your parents, but I'm very
excited about the fact

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:49.102
that you play
Eddie Murphy's daughter

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.003
in the "Coming to America"
sequel

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.538
that will be
coming out soon.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.673
How was that?
I mean,

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:56.976
I can't tell you how
jealous I am of the fact

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:59.312
that you got to be on a set
with Eddie Murphy

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:02.315
and Wesley Snipes and Arsenio.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.050
So tell me what it was like.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.819
-Man, it was -- I mean,
it was incredible.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:10.056
I mean, I was surrounded by
people who are truly

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.525
masters of their craft.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.295
And just being able to sit back,

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.931
and watch, and absorb
and learn from that,

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:21.567
I mean, I'm very grateful,
you know, that this early

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.570
in my career, I get this type
of exposure to, you know,

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:28.141
these really -- I mean,
masters at their craft.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:31.110
And actually, I do kick a --

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.646
I do kick a little ass
in "Coming to America."

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.014
I will just say that.
-Oh, good to know!

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.350
Good to know! A little --
another spoiler alert.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.719
[ Laughter ]
-...just slide that in there.

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:42.055
-Uh-oh.
I mean, at this point,

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.455
it would be a waste
of your talents

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:45.324
to not let you kick a little ass
in a movie.

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:47.360
Just a little bit if somebody
gets out of line.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.929
-Yeah.
-Is it -- Was it --

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.764
I mean, obviously there's
still work to do

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.099
when you're on a movie set,
but was the atmosphere

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:56.369
celebratory that
everybody was back together

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.037
making this beloved movie again?

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.906
-Very much so.
Very, very much so.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:04.243
So it was great to be in that
energy as well.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.578
And I mean, it's such a classic,

00:04:06.578 --> 00:04:09.681
and these are all people
that love that first film,

00:04:09.681 --> 00:04:11.017
love working together.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.085
And so, you know,
just to be able to

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:17.256
witness kind of this
family reunion of sorts

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:22.027
and then to be invited to be
a part of that family --

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:25.164
I mean, yeah, it's special.
It's so special.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.366
-How old do you think you were
when you saw

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.268
the first "Coming to America?"

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:32.705
-Ooh, I would have been way
younger than I should have been

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:33.939
to be watching.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:35.374
-I feel like a lot of
people saw that movie

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.443
when they were too young.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:42.481
-Probably somewhere between
like 8 and 10,

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:45.151
because it's my eldest brother's
favorite movie.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.919
So, the first time I would
have watched it

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.421
would have been with him,
and, yeah.

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:50.622
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:50.622 --> 00:04:52.892
That's the price
of older siblings.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.861
You sometimes see stuff
a little too early.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.729
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.463
-Hey, thanks so much
for being here.

00:04:58.463 --> 00:04:59.898
Congrats on the film.

00:04:59.898 --> 00:05:03.101
Such a delight to speak
with you and to meet you.

00:05:03.101 --> 00:05:05.305
-Thank you.
Same to you, Seth.

